# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. Ingestion decides what to re-embed by hashing each file's
# contents, so a checkout that turned 142 corpus files into CRLF would change all 142
# hashes. The first ingest on that machine would re-embed the whole corpus, and the
# incremental path, which is the interesting part, would have nothing to demonstrate.
# Git's default on Windows is core.autocrlf=true, so that is the machine most likely to
# clone this next.
#
# No binary rules below. Every one of the 322 tracked files is text, *.pdf is gitignored
# on purpose so the case document is never committed, and `text=auto` leaves anything git
# detects as binary alone. Rules for file types that are not here would be guesses.
* text=auto eol=lf
